Falsifies `machine_statistics_contract::verification::a_built_header_reads_back_as_an_empty_page`.

The defect: `build_header` writes the frame size into the tick-rate word, so a reader prints
times at the wrong rate. A host test that builds a header with the frame size equal to the tick
rate would not see it; the harness takes both as arbitrary values.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(s.tick_hertz, tick_hertz)`.

diff --git a/crates/machine_statistics_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/machine_statistics_contract/src/lib.rs
index d70573b6e..3c65a6ca8 100644
--- a/crates/machine_statistics_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/machine_statistics_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@ pub fn build_header(frame_bytes: u64, tick_hertz: u64) -> [u64; word::LINE_WORDS
     line[word::header::MAGIC] = u64::from_le_bytes(MAGIC);
     line[word::header::VERSION] = u64::from(VERSION);
     line[word::header::FRAME_BYTES] = frame_bytes;
-    line[word::header::TICK_HERTZ] = tick_hertz;
+    line[word::header::TICK_HERTZ] = frame_bytes;
     line
 }
 
